    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nAn extension type that inherits from another extension type in the same module can be given the vectorcall form of `tp_new` while its base class is generated with only the plain form, without the vectorcall. In this case the base class only has `__pyx_tp_new_<module>_<Base>` defined, but the derived type's generated `tp_new_vectorcall` calls `__pyx_tp_new_vectorcall_<module>_<Base>`.\n\nThe C compiler warns it as an implicit declaration, then warns about an `int`-to-pointer assignment, but the link of the shared object succeeds, and the failure surfaces at import:\n\n```\nImportError: .../repro.cpython-314-x86_64-linux-gnu.so: undefined symbol: __pyx_tp_new_vectorcall_5repro_Base\n```\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n**`repro.pyx`**:\n\n```cython\ncdef class Base:\n    cdef object payload\n\n    def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        raise RuntimeError(\"This class cannot be instantiated directly.\")\n\n\ncdef class Leaf(Base):\n    cdef object extra\n\n    def __init__(self, x):\n        self.extra = x\n```\n\n``` bash\n... $ cythonize -i repro.pyx\nCompiling .../repro.pyx because it changed.\n[1/1] Cythonizing .../repro.pyx\n.../repro.c: In function ‘__pyx_tp_new_vectorcall_5repro_Leaf’:\n.../repro.c:4834:7: warning: implicit declaration of function ‘__pyx_tp_new_vectorcall_5repro_Base’; did you mean ‘__pyx_tp_new_vectorcall_5repro_Leaf’? [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]\n 4834 |   o = __pyx_tp_new_vectorcall_5repro_Base(t,\n      |       ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n      |       __pyx_tp_new_vectorcall_5repro_Leaf\n.../repro.c:4834:5: warning: assignment to ‘PyObject *’ {aka ‘struct _object *’} from ‘int’ makes pointer from integer without a cast [-Wint-conversion]\n 4834 |   o = __pyx_tp_new_vectorcall_5repro_Base(t,\n      |     ^\n... $ ls *.so\nrepro.cpython-314-x86_64-linux-gnu.so\n... $ python -c \"import repro\"\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import repro\nImportError: .../repro.cpython-314-x86_64-linux-gnu.so: undefined symbol: __pyx_tp_new_vectorcall_5repro_Base\n... $ nm -u repro*.so | grep repro\n                 U __pyx_tp_new_vectorcall_5repro_Base\n```\n\nRemoving the attributes (`payload`, `extra` above) causes the call to an undefined function to occur in a `__pyx_tp_vectorcall_...` function rather than a `__pyx_tp_new_vectorcall_...` function.\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nThe derived class references a function the module defines, and import of the module succeeds.\n\n### OS\n\nLinux x86_64, gcc 13\n\n### Python version\n\n3.14\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0\n\n### Additional context\n\nAs a workaround, adding a `__cinit__` that can't be a vectorcall to the deriving class resolves this: \n\n``` cython\ncdef class Leaf(Base):\n    cdef object extra\n\n    def __cinit__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        pass\n\n    def __init__(self, x):\n        self.extra = x\n```\n\nThis compiles without warning and can be imported as normal, and `nm -u repro*.so | grep repro` reports nothing.",
